WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:03.730
Something didn't go the way you hoped for.

00:03.730 --> 00:08.000
To keep it real, it didn't work.

00:08.000 --> 00:13.450
You have something else that needs your full attention, and it's in 15 minutes.

00:13.450 --> 00:19.100
Before you decide what to do next, what is still with you from what just happened?

00:19.100 --> 00:21.300
Name it, even if briefly.

00:36.450 --> 00:41.900
How long does the last moment control the next one?

00:41.900 --> 00:44.300
That's reset speed.

00:44.300 --> 00:49.300
And like an athlete's recovery between reps, it can be conditioned.

00:49.300 --> 00:51.250
Here are your options.

00:51.250 --> 00:54.200
Delay or cancel what's next.

00:54.200 --> 00:57.400
Show up and act like nothing happened.

00:57.400 --> 01:01.100
Show up, name it briefly and move forward.

01:01.100 --> 01:04.800
Show up and let the frustration spill into it.

01:15.800 --> 01:20.700
One more thing just went wrong, right on top of this.

01:20.700 --> 01:22.050
What do you do now?

01:27.950 --> 01:29.700
Time yourself this week.

01:29.700 --> 01:38.700
Take note: after something goes wrong, how long before you're fully present for the next thing on your plate?

01:38.700 --> 01:42.700
Try to shorten the gap.
